<newsitem itemid="416033" id="root" date="1997-03-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Newman Tonks year profit up before charge.</title>
<headline>Newman Tonks year profit up before charge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) loss	 0.47		   vs 14.11 profit</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.4		    vs N/A</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 8.025		  vs 6.9</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    6.3		    vs 27.2 profit</p>
<p> Turnover		   270.9		  vs 277.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Above results include a charge of 11.8 million stg in 1996 related to discontinued operations versus a credit of 10.1 million stg a year earlier. Excluding exceptionals, pretax profit was 18.1 million stg versus 17.1 million stg.</p>
<p>Newman Tonks Group Plc said the results were in line with the profit estimates made at the time of Ingersoll-Rand Co's recommended offer for the company.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
